noBrainNotice
	🧠 No brain is set up for this chat yet. Open the bridge dashboard and add one.
heldBrainNotice
	🧠 The brain for this chat cannot run right now. The Brains page of the bridge dashboard says why.
restartedNotice
	🔄 I restarted while I was working on your message. Send it again if you still need an answer.
resetReply(false)
	✅ Cleared anything this chat had running or waiting.
resetReply(true)
	✅ Reset. I stopped what this chat had running or waiting, and the next message starts without its earlier messages. What I noted in my memory files stays.
stopReply(true, 0)
	🛑 Stopped, and cleared anything this chat had waiting.
stopReply(false, 2)
	🛑 Nothing was running for this chat; cleared what it had waiting.
stopReply(false, 0)
	🛑 Nothing was running for this chat.
helpReply("")
	🤖 *Fridolin*

	Send a message to talk to Claude. Images, documents, audio, and video are passed along as files.

	*Commands:*
	• `!help` — show this help
	• `!stop` — stop what I'm doing for this chat and drop its queued messages
	• `!reset` — like `!stop`, and the next message starts without this chat's earlier messages
	• `!fleet` — the machines connected to me as nodes (direct chats only)
	• `!lockdown` — owner only: pause all work but reading until `!unlock`
helpReply("@claude")
	🤖 *Fridolin*

	Send a message to talk to Claude. Images, documents, audio, and video are passed along as files.

	*Commands:*
	• `!help` — show this help
	• `!stop` — stop what I'm doing for this chat and drop its queued messages
	• `!reset` — like `!stop`, and the next message starts without this chat's earlier messages
	• `!fleet` — the machines connected to me as nodes (direct chats only)
	• `!lockdown` — owner only: pause all work but reading until `!unlock`

	In this group, start your message with `@claude` or reply to one of mine to address me, commands included.
queuedNotice(2)
	⏳ Queued (#2) — I'll get to this right after the current task.
queueFullNotice("@claude !stop")
	⏳ I'm still busy with earlier messages and my queue is full. Try again in a bit, or send `@claude !stop` to drop what this chat has waiting.
otpCaughtNotice
	🔐 That looks like the one-time code this chat was asked for, so I kept it out of the conversation: the assistant does not see it.
workingNotice
	⏳ Working on it...
questionPrefix
	❓ Which day?
chatErrNotSignedIn
	🔑 Claude is not signed in on the bridge machine. Run `claude` there once and log in, then send your message again.
chatErrCodexNotSignedIn
	🔑 Codex is not signed in for this brain. See the bridge dashboard for its sign-in command, then send your message again.
chatErrCodexLimit
	⏳ Codex's usage limit is reached for now. Try again later.
chatErrLimit
	⏳ Claude's usage limit is reached for now. Try again later.
chatErrTimeout
	⌛ That took too long and was stopped. Try again, perhaps with a smaller request.
chatErrGeneric
	❌ Something went wrong — details on the bridge dashboard.
chatErrSandbox
	❌ The sandbox could not be set up.
chatErrClaude
	❌ Claude: Credit balance is too low
chatErrCodex
	❌ Codex: Something failed
buildChatError
	❌ brain queue is full
viewOnceNotice
	👁️ I don't open view-once photos, videos or voice notes: I would keep them. Send it as a normal one if I should see it.
mediaTooLargeNotice
	⚠️ That file is over the 100 MB limit, so I skipped it.
mediaFailedNotice
	⚠️ I couldn't download that file. Please send it again.
pollAsText
	📊 *Lunch on Friday?*
	1. Pizza
	2. Sushi
startupCheckAlert
	⚠️ Bridge startup check: missing ~/.fridolin/credentials/google_calendar_token_main.json
backupRefusedAlert
	⚠️ Backup of Notes: it would delete 12 of 40 files

	Check the brain folder, then the Backup page in the Fridolin dashboard. Scheduled backups of this brain keep refusing until one succeeds; this is the only message about it.
plaudGivenUpAlert
	⚠️ Plaud: the recording “Team sync” was not handed to brain notes: brain notes is not configured. It is still in Plaud, and the dashboard lists it (Integrations → Plaud).
plaudExpiredAlert
	⚠️ Plaud: the login expired, so new recordings are not arriving. Reconnect in the Fridolin dashboard (Integrations → Plaud).
fleetGroupNotice
	🖥️ !fleet answers only in a direct chat.
fleetReply(false)
	🖥️ Nodes are off. Turn on nodes.enabled in the config and restart the bridge to connect other machines (docs/NODES.md).
fleetReply(true, none)
	🖥️ No nodes yet. On the core, run `fridolin nodes join-code` and paste the line it prints on the new machine.
